 {"version_id": "struct-09", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Type-normalizing and exception-safe edit-command boundary", "target_failure_mode": "Brittle output and orchestration handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["django__django-15213", "django__django-12747", "django__django-13768", "django__django-11964"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "kgcompass/repair.py", "find": "def parse_diff_edit_commands_strict(*args, **kwargs):\n    try:\n        return _parse_diff_edit_commands_strict(*args, **kwargs)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, IndexError):\n        return []", "replace": "def parse_diff_edit_commands_strict(*args, **kwargs):\n    try:\n        parsed = _parse_diff_edit_commands_strict(*args, **kwargs)\n    except Exception:\n        return []\n    if parsed is None:\n        return []\n    if isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        parsed = [parsed]\n    if not isinstance(parsed, list):\n        return []\n    return [item for item in parsed if isinstance(item, dict) and item]"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.68, "reasoning_soundness": 0.61, "execution_accuracy": 0.58, "output_integrity": 0.68}, "aggregate": 0.6375, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "django__django-15213", "score": 0.9}, {"instance_id": "django__django-12747", "score": 0.9}, {"instance_id": "django__django-13768", "score": 0.23}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11964", "score": 0.24}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.01, "why": "Normalizing parser outputs and preventing boundary exceptions improves orchestration robustness. However, converting unexpected parser failures into empty edit lists can silently discard valid edits, so execution accuracy and reasoning soundness remain near baseline and are slightly penalized."}
 {"version_id": "struct-10", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Post-application transactional diff validation", "target_failure_mode": "Patch generation and application failures", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["django__django-15213", "django__django-12747", "django__django-13768", "django__django-11964"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "kgcompass/repair.py", "find": "from utils import (\n    format_entity_content,\n    extract_python_blocks,\n    split_edit_multifile_commands,\n    parse_diff_edit_commands_strict as _parse_diff_edit_commands_strict,\n    check_syntax,\n    applable_patch,\n)", "replace": "from utils import (\n    format_entity_content,\n    extract_python_blocks,\n    split_edit_multifile_commands,\n    parse_diff_edit_commands_strict as _parse_diff_edit_commands_strict,\n    check_syntax,\n    applable_patch as _applable_patch,\n)\n\ndef applable_patch(*args, **kwargs):\n    result = _applable_patch(*args, **kwargs)\n    if not result:\n        return result\n    verified = subprocess.run(\n   "}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.68, "reasoning_soundness": 0.64, "execution_accuracy": 0.63, "output_integrity": 0.67}, "aggregate": 0.655, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "django__django-15213", "score": 0.92}, {"instance_id": "django__django-12747", "score": 0.91}, {"instance_id": "django__django-13768", "score": 0.32}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11964", "score": 0.35}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0275, "why": "Transactional post-application validation most directly addresses patch application failures by rejecting or containing invalid edits and checking the resulting state. It substantially improves execution accuracy and modestly improves reasoning soundness, with some risk of rejecting marginally valid patches."}
 {"version_id": "struct-11", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Optional provider imports for single-provider execution", "target_failure_mode": "Brittle output and orchestration handling", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["django__django-15213", "django__django-12747", "django__django-13768", "django__django-11964"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "kgcompass/repair_claude.py", "find": "import anthropic", "replace": "try:\n    import anthropic\nexcept ImportError:\n    anthropic = None"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.68, "reasoning_soundness": 0.62, "execution_accuracy": 0.57, "output_integrity": 0.66}, "aggregate": 0.6325, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "django__django-15213", "score": 0.9}, {"instance_id": "django__django-12747", "score": 0.9}, {"instance_id": "django__django-13768", "score": 0.21}, {"instance_id": "django__django-11964", "score": 0.2}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.005, "why": "Making the Anthropic import optional helps environments that do not install every provider, but this single-provider execution change does not address localization, patch generation, or benchmark reasoning. It provides only a small orchestration benefit and may defer failure until provider use."}
